# SYNTAX TEST "text.html.tiddlywiki5" "A minted attribute or parameter name never leaks into a scope"

# RULED 2026-09-21: `meta.attribute.widget.$1`, `meta.attribute.unrecognized.$1` and the call
# parameter's `…parameter.tw-$1…` interpolated raw author text into a scope name. An attribute
# name TiddlyWiki accepts with punctuation — `(a`, `$x`, `a.b` — mints a segment no TextMate
# selector can ever target (VS Code selects by dot-bounded prefix only), and no bundled theme
# paints `meta.*` regardless, so per-name targeting bought nobody anything. The widget and
# unrecognized attribute catch-alls now carry FIXED names; the parameter's segment holds only for
# a clean `[\w\-]+` word (which is all it ever captures) and falls back to a fixed
# `tw-positional` name where the call carries no name at all — never a dangling `tw-`.

! A widget attribute opening on punctuation mints no segment

<$button (a="x">c</$button>
#        ^^ meta.attribute.widget.html.tiddlywiki5 entity.other.attribute-name.html.tiddlywiki5

! A widget attribute opening on a dollar mints no segment either

<$link $x="y">c</$link>
#      ^^ meta.attribute.widget.html.tiddlywiki5 entity.other.attribute-name.html.tiddlywiki5

! An unrecognized HTML attribute reads the same fixed name

<div a.b="x">c</div>
#    ^^^ meta.attribute.unrecognized.html.tiddlywiki5 entity.other.attribute-name.html.tiddlywiki5

! A positional call parameter reads a fixed fallback, never a dangling `tw-`

<<a=b>>
#  ^^ meta.variable.procedure.parameter.tw-positional.tiddlywiki5 string.unquoted.html.tiddlywiki5

! A control: a NAMED call parameter still carries its own clean-word name

<<myproc argname:"v">>
#        ^^^^^^^ meta.variable.procedure.parameter.tw-argname.tiddlywiki5 variable.parameter.tiddlywiki5
